<worksheet >
    <title>LSAI-4 Application of Linear Systems</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>To earn an M on this outcome, complete both problems. Complete one problem with progress on the other to earn a P.</p>
  </introduction>  
  <page>
    <exercise workspace="1.75in">
        <introduction><p>A network of one-way streets is shown in the figure below.</p>
         <image source="flow_pattern_3.png" width="50%" margins="0% 50%" />
        </introduction>
      <task><statement><p>Set up a system of linear equations using the variables <m>x_1, x_2, x_3, x_4</m> 
        corresponding to the flow at each intersection.</p></statement></task>
      <task><statement><p>Assuming that all of the flows are non-negative, find a general solution to 
        the system.</p></statement></task>
      <task><statement><p>Assuming that all of the flows are non-negative, find a specific solution to 
        the system with the smallest possible value for <m>x_4</m>.</p></statement></task>
    </exercise>
  </page>
  <page>
    <exercise workspace="1.5in">
          <introduction><p>Consider the chemical reaction: <md>CO_2 + H_2O \to C_6H_{12}O_6 + O_2</md></p></introduction>
      <task><statement><p>Set up a system of linear equations to represent this chemical reaction.</p></statement></task>
        <task><statement><p>Balance the chemical equation. Support your answer.</p></statement></task>
    </exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>